  "sport": "soccer",
  "title": "Look up and pass in pairs",
  "description": "Mark out a rectangle of about 30 × 40 metres with no goals. The players work in pairs with one ball per pair. Everyone keeps moving around the area and passes with their partner, while the other pairs run and pass in all directions.\n\nBefore the pass is played, passer and receiver must make eye contact. The receiver shows in a free space and the passer waits for the right moment, when no other player or ball is in the way. Start at walking pace and speed up as you go.\n\nVariation: both players in the pair have a ball and pass to each other at the same time. Both have to look up and pick the same moment. More pairs in the same area makes it harder. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Look up before the ball arrives – know where your partner is and where the others are going."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Look for eye contact and only pass when you see each other."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Take the ball on with your first touch and look up again straight away."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Receiver: keep moving and show where the passing lane is clear."
    }
  ],
